WHAT YOU CAN DO

You can install and use SchutzelDev on any computer you control, for personal or
work use, including commercial projects you are allowed to work on.

SchutzelDev is currently free. Future versions may be paid, but any version you
already have will continue to work under the terms that came with it.

WHAT YOU CAN'T DO

You may not redistribute, resell, sublicense, rent, or host SchutzelDev for other
people.

You may not decompile or reverse engineer the distributed software, except where
the law gives you that right.

You may not remove or change copyright or attribution notices.

You may not use SchutzelDev to build a competing product from its internals.

WORKING WITH YOUR CODE

SchutzelDev can suggest changes to files in the directory you run it from and its
subdirectories.

Before a suggested code change is written, SchutzelDev shows you the proposed diff
and asks for your approval. Model-provided file changes are restricted to the
directory SchutzelDev is run from and its subdirectories.

You should run SchutzelDev from the root directory of the project you want to work
on. Please review proposed changes before accepting them and keep your work in
version control or otherwise backed up.

SchutzelDev uses a local language model. Like any AI model, it can make mistakes,
so you should review its output before relying on it.

